---
// "The short version": five plain points and four numbers, for readers who won't scroll.
// Matches the ash band in design/approved-mockup.html.
//
// Design note: every point and number can be checked against the capstone's documents:
//   [1] 3 vs 10 days ........ project-context/1.define/mrd.md (lead-time table)
//   [3] no "approve all" .... capstone-brief.md, prd.md §6
//   [4] dates by code ....... prd.md ("Date calculation is not an agent responsibility")
//   [5] / 22 deadlines ...... mock-data/expected-obligation-library.md §4
//   30 min target ........... prd.md (specialist time, under 30 minutes)
---

<!-- id="short" is where the hero's "Read the short version" button jumps to -->
<section id="short" class="scroll-mt-6 bg-ash py-14 md:py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 md:px-10">
    <div class="grid gap-6 min-[900px]:grid-cols-[320px_1fr] min-[900px]:gap-15">
      <div>
        <p class="mb-3.5 font-display text-[13px] leading-[1.38] tracking-[-0.01em] text-brass">About two minutes</p>
        <h2 class="text-[40px] leading-[1.1]">The short version</h2>
      </div>

      <ol data-note="Short version|Five plain points for readers who won’t scroll, written for someone outside finance. Each one can be checked against the project documents." class="grid gap-6">
        <li class="point">
          <span class="num">[1]</span>
          <span>Today a compliance specialist reads the law and types every reporting deadline into a spreadsheet by hand. Mistakes slip in: two of the team’s own documents give the same monthly report different lead times, 3 days and 10 days.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="point">
          <span class="num">[2]</span>
          <span>In my tool, AI agents do the first reading of the law. Every rule they pull out must quote the exact sentence it came from, and a second AI agent checks that the quote is real.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="point">
          <span class="num">[3]</span>
          <span>A human specialist then approves each rule, one at a time, at three checkpoints. There is <strong>no “approve all” button</strong>, and nothing is approved by default.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="point">
          <span class="num">[4]</span>
          <span>The deadlines themselves are worked out by ordinary code, not by AI, so the same input always gives the same date.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="point">
          <span class="num">[5]</span>
          <span>Before building anything, I wrote an answer key: the exact results the tool should produce, down to all 22 deadlines. Every test run will be marked against it.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Design note: every number is a claim someone can check in the repo. White data cards on
         ash, with ember used only as a short line (never as text). -->
    <div data-note="Numbers|Every number is a claim someone can check in the capstone’s documents. White data cards on ash, with ember used only as a short line." class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-2 gap-5 min-[860px]:grid-cols-4">
      <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="rule"></span><b>3</b><span>checkpoints where a person signs off</span></div>
      <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="rule"></span><b>0</b><span>deadlines calculated by AI</span></div>
      <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="rule"></span><b>22</b><span>deadlines in the answer key</span></div>
      <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="rule"></span><b>30<small>min</small></b><span>target time for a person to review the AI’s work</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ---------- The five points ---------- */
  .point {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr; gap: 12px;
    font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-steel);
  }
  .num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-brass); padding-top: 4px; }
  .point strong { color: var(--color-graphite); font-weight: 500; }

  /* ---------- The four numbers ---------- */
  .stat { background: var(--color-canvas-white); border-radius: 20px; padding: 28px 24px; }
  .stat b {
    display: block; margin-bottom: 14px;
    font: 400 clamp(44px, 4.6vw, 60px)/1 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .stat b small { font-size: 0.38em; letter-spacing: 0; margin-left: 4px; }
  .stat > span:last-child { display: block; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.43; color: var(--color-steel); }

  /* The short ember line draws itself when the card scrolls into view.
     "is-in" is added by the reveal script in Base.astro. */
  .rule {
    display: block; height: 2px; width: 28px; margin-bottom: 22px; background: var(--color-ember);
    transition: width 700ms var(--ease-out-soft);
  }
  /* Waiting to scroll into view: line not drawn yet */
  :global(.reveal-ready:not(.is-in)) .rule { width: 0; }
</style>
